{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 343 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "53da9e2a127806300c5aeebabdaa90a1e8935015a16fc78f6b3c6fba16d97874" :edb/db-before-t 342 :edb/db-after-t 343 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533655 50 #inst "2026-10-04T07:15:15.916Z" 13194139533655 true] [17592186087781 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244442 13194139533655 true] [17592186087781 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244452 13194139533655 true] [17592186087781 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244467 13194139533655 true] [17592186087781 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244474 13194139533655 true] [17592186087781 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244509 13194139533655 true] [17592186087782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244457 13194139533655 true] [17592186087782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244463 13194139533655 true] [17592186087782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244481 13194139533655 true] [17592186087782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244488 13194139533655 true] [17592186087782 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244523 13194139533655 true] [17592186087783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244421 13194139533655 true] [17592186087783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244448 13194139533655 true] [17592186087783 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244516 13194139533655 true] [17592186087784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244428 13194139533655 true] [17592186087784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244435 13194139533655 true] [17592186087784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244495 13194139533655 true] [17592186087784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244502 13194139533655 true] [17592186087784 1020 #edb/ref 17592186244530 13194139533655 true] [17592186088105 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533655 true] [17592186088105 1145 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+x} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\nx({x}^{2}+x+1)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $2x=0$ gives the solution $x=0.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+x+1=0$ has no real solutions because the discriminant $D$ is negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & ={1}^{2}-4(1)(1) \\\\  & =1-4 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only vertical asymptote is $x=0.$" 13194139533655 true] [17592186088328 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533655 true] [17592186088328 1145 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-4x+5=0.\n$$\n\nNote that the above equation has no real solutions because the discriminant $D$ is negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & =(-4{)}^{2}-4(1)(5) \\\\  & =16-20 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes." 13194139533655 true] [17592186244421 1017 #edb/ref 17592186244422 13194139533655 true] [17592186244421 1089 "q-113527" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244421 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533655 true] [17592186244421 1100 "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-12}.$" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244421 1113 #uuid "046b8096-a4b3-5639-81fd-05cfaf3fcc14" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244421 1138 false 13194139533655 true] [17592186244421 1145 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-12} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{{x}^{2}(x-2)+6(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{({x}^{2}+6)(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+6)(x-2)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $x-2=0$ gives the solution $x=2.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+6=0$ has no real solutions.\n\nTherefore, the only vertical asymptote is $x=2.$" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244423 13194139533655 true] [17592186244422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244424 13194139533655 true] [17592186244422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244425 13194139533655 true] [17592186244422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244426 13194139533655 true] [17592186244422 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244427 13194139533655 true] [17592186244422 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533655 true] [17592186244422 1041 "selection" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244422 1104 #edb/ref 17592186244425 13194139533655 true] [17592186244422 1110 #uuid "aff3477f-6944-59c3-b10c-0345d482afc7" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244423 1034 "$x=0$ and $x=2$" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244423 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533655 true] [17592186244423 1111 #uuid "e07bcdb7-1b3b-5227-8965-90e8e187ede5" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244424 1034 "$x=6$ only" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244424 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533655 true] [17592186244424 1111 #uuid "d1c605ad-69c9-580d-8218-af950816c14b" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244425 1034 "$x=2$ only" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244425 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533655 true] [17592186244425 1111 #uuid "2112feaf-e9d9-5a3d-ae9a-465d4aa43900" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244426 1034 "$x=-6$ only" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244426 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533655 true] [17592186244426 1111 #uuid "0ed3e03b-2b97-5daa-af26-00ec3fa514f8" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244427 1034 "$x=2$ and $x=6$ only" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533655 true] [17592186244427 1111 #uuid "d964613e-fcda-5f09-8c63-a405fd222a5d" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244428 1017 #edb/ref 17592186244429 13194139533655 true] [17592186244428 1089 "q-113545" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244428 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533655 true] [17592186244428 1100 "Calculate the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}.$" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244428 1113 #uuid "95984799-323b-581e-b3cf-2bbb458bdbef" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244428 1138 false 13194139533655 true] [17592186244428 1145 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}({x}^{2}+x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}+x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x+2=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions because the discriminant $D$ is negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & =1-4(1)(2) \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes." 13194139533655 true] [17592186244429 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244430 13194139533655 true] [17592186244429 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244431 13194139533655 true] [17592186244429 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244432 13194139533655 true] [17592186244429 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244433 13194139533655 true] [17592186244429 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244434 13194139533655 true] [17592186244429 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533655 true] [17592186244429 1041 "selection" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244429 1104 #edb/ref 17592186244434 13194139533655 true] [17592186244429 1110 #uuid "7741aef8-3d0c-58eb-8091-17b7b76f794b" 13194139533655 true] 