 13194139533655 true] [17592186244449 1041 "field-1" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244449 1104 #edb/ref 17592186244451 13194139533655 true] [17592186244449 1110 #uuid "151a1256-0239-5a7c-9590-a11ed93d9436" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244450 1034 "-4" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244450 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533655 true] [17592186244450 1111 #uuid "ec861ded-03c9-5f56-bfe6-21787fd8f3b5" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244451 1034 "4" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244451 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533655 true] [17592186244451 1111 #uuid "f17f0b1f-6926-5b07-afaf-eb5245098b37" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244452 1017 #edb/ref 17592186244453 13194139533655 true] [17592186244452 1017 #edb/ref 17592186244455 13194139533655 true] [17592186244452 1089 "q-278534" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244452 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533655 true] [17592186244452 1100 "In **ascending order**, the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{x+5}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533655 true] [17592186244452 1113 #uuid "7c02d208-ab50-59ab-9034-5180c0ab1f28" 13194139533655 true] [17592186244452 1138 false 13194139533655 true] [17592186244452 1145 "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nAdding both fractions and then factoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{x+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+5)+(x-1)}{(x-1)(x+5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+10+x-1}{(x-1)(x+5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x+9}{(x-1)(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)(x+5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the two solutions $x=-5$ and $x=1.$ \n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the equations of the vertical asymptotes are $